  "title_en": "Mistake Clinic: Fix the Tones",
  "title_py": "Cuòwù mén zhěn: gǎizhèng shēngdiào",
  "category": "Tones / food / family",
  "hsk": 1,
  "date": "2026-11-25",
  "auditory_note": "Tap ▶ Listen to play each clip.",
  "teach": {
    "intro": {
      "en": "Hi Evan! Today is a mistake clinic with no new words. We look at the tone slips from recent report cards, see why each one happens, and practice the fixes.",
      "py": "Nǐ hǎo, Evan! Jīntiān shì cuòwù mén zhěn, méiyǒu xīn cí. Wǒmen kàn zuìjìn chéngjì dān shàng de shēngdiào cuò, kàn měi gè cuò wèishénme fāshēng, ránhòu liànxí gǎizhèng."
    },
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Mistake clinic: fix the tones that slipped"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "en": "Today is a mistake clinic with no new words. I looked at your last report cards, and the words are almost always right. What slips is the tone mark. So we take each slip, say why it happens, and fix it with the sound in your ear.",
        "py": "Jīntiān shì cuòwù mén zhěn, méiyǒu xīn cí. Wǒ kànle nǐ zuìjìn de chéngjì dān, cí jīhū dōu duì, cuò de shì shēngdiào. Suǒyǐ wǒmen bǎ měi gè cuò dōu názhe, shuō yuányīn, ránhòu yòng shēngyīn gǎizhèng."
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Slip 1: third tone dips (niúnǎi, nǐ hǎo, hěn, jǐ)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "en": "Third tone goes down and then up. Earlier answers wrote niúnài, nihāo, hen and jī. The fix: when you hear a low dipping sound, write the little cup mark ˇ.",
        "py": "Dì-sān shēng xiān jiàng hòu shēng. Zhīqián xiěguo niúnài, nihāo, hen hé jī. Gǎizhèng: tīngdào dī ér wān de shēngyīn jiù xiě ˇ."
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "milk",
        "py": "niúnǎi",
        "note_en": "Niú is 2nd tone, nǎi is 3rd tone with the cup.",
        "note_py": "Niú shì dì-èr shēng, nǎi shì dì-sān shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-niunai.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "hello",
        "py": "nǐ hǎo",
        "note_en": "Two 3rd tones in a row: the first sounds like 2nd (ní hǎo) but you still write nǐ hǎo.",
        "note_py": "Liǎng gè dì-sān shēng: dì-yī gè tīng qǐlái xiàng dì-èr shēng, dàn hái shì xiě nǐ hǎo.",
        "listen_url": "l23-nihao.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "very",
        "py": "hěn",
        "note_en": "Hěn is 3rd tone, with the cup mark.",
        "note_py": "Hěn shì dì-sān shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-hen.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "how many",
        "py": "jǐ",
        "note_en": "Jǐ is 3rd tone. Jī (1st) would be a different word.",
        "note_py": "Jǐ shì dì-sān shēng. Jī shì dì-yī shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-ji.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Slip 2: tea, meat and thank you (chá, ròu, xièxie)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "en": "Chá rises like a question (2nd tone), but chā was written. Ròu drops sharply (4th tone), but rǒu was written. Xièxie starts with a falling 4th tone, not a rising one.",
        "py": "Chá shàngshēng xiàng wèn wèntí (dì-èr shēng), dàn xiěchéngle chā. Ròu jíjù xiàjiàng (dì-sì shēng), dàn xiěchéngle rǒu. Xièxie yǐ dì-sì shēng kāishǐ, bú shì dì-èr shēng."
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "tea",
        "py": "chá",
        "note_en": "Rising: like asking 'huh?'",
        "note_py": "Shàngshēng: xiàng wèn 'á?'",
        "listen_url": "l23-cha.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "meat",
        "py": "ròu",
        "note_en": "Falling sharply: like saying 'no!'",
        "note_py": "Jíjù xiàjiàng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-rou.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "thank you",
        "py": "xièxie",
        "note_en": "Xiè is 4th tone, the second xie is light and short.",
        "note_py": "Xiè shì dì-sì shēng, dì-èr gè xie qīngshēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-xiexie.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Slip 3: sì versus sí, and the spelling of miànbāo"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "four",
        "py": "sì",
        "note_en": "Sì is 4th tone, sharp and falling.",
        "note_py": "Sì shì dì-sì shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-si.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "bread",
        "py": "miànbāo",
        "note_en": "Spell it m-i-à-n: the tone mark goes on the a. Miàn is 4th tone, bāo is 1st.",
        "note_py": "Pīn chéng m-i-à-n: shēngdiào biāo zài a shàng. Miàn dì-sì shēng, bāo dì-yī shēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-mianbao.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "vocab_card",
        "en": "older sister",
        "py": "jiějie",
        "note_en": "Jiě is 3rd tone, the second jie is light and has no mark.",
        "note_py": "Jiě shì dì-sān shēng, dì-èr gè jie shì qīngshēng.",
        "listen_url": "l23-jiejie.mp3"
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Slip 4: bù, not bú"
      },
      {
        "type": "callout",
        "kind": "tone",
        "title": "Rule: bù, but bú before a 4th tone",
        "body_en": "Bù is 4th tone by itself: wǒ bù hē niúnǎi (I don't drink milk). Only before another 4th tone does it change to bú: bú shì. Hē is 1st tone, so it stays bù.",
        "body_py": "Bù běnlái shì dì-sì shēng: wǒ bù hē niúnǎi. Zhǐyǒu zài lìng yí gè dì-sì shēng qián cái biànchéng bú: bú shì. Hē shì dì-yī shēng, suǒyǐ hái shì bù."
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "I don't drink milk.",
        "py": "Wǒ bù hē niúnǎi.",
        "listen_url": "l23-e1.mp3",
        "n": 1
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "I don't eat meat.",
        "py": "Wǒ bù chī ròu.",
        "listen_url": "l23-e2.mp3",
        "n": 2
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "Do you drink tea?",
        "py": "Nǐ hē chá ma?",
        "listen_url": "l23-e3.mp3",
        "n": 3
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "My older sister drinks tea.",
        "py": "Wǒ de jiějie hē chá.",
        "listen_url": "l23-e4.mp3",
        "n": 4
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "I eat four apples.",
        "py": "Wǒ chī sì gè píngguǒ.",
        "listen_url": "l23-e5.mp3",
        "n": 5
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "en": "Thank you, goodbye!",
        "py": "Xièxie, zàijiàn!",
        "listen_url": "l23-e6.mp3",
        "n": 6
      }
    ]
  },
